th=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"102.6\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#B8912F\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">$179.51</tspan> your 2.618 ext</text><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"126.5\" y2=\"126.5\" stroke=\"#1B8FA8\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"130.5\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1B8FA8\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">$174.69</tspan> your 2.382 ext</text><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"171.6\" y2=\"171.6\" stroke=\"#20242C\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" class=\"l-white\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"175.6\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#20242C\" class=\"t-white\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">$166.89</tspan> your 2.0 ext</text><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"216.7\" y2=\"216.7\" stroke=\"#B8912F\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"220.7\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#B8912F\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">$159.09</tspan> your 1.618 ext</text><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"244.6\" y2=\"244.6\" stroke=\"#1B8FA8\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"248.6\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1B8FA8\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">$154.27</tspan> your 1.382 ext</text><circle cx=\"515.1\" cy=\"172.6\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#C9A84C\" stroke=\"#20242C\" stroke-width=\"1\"/></svg></figure>\n<p>These are your own extension levels from your Nov 7 drawing, unchanged.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Trend:</strong> Close $166.71 (Nov 11). Below the 20-day ($175.99) and the 50-day ($169.10), above the rising 200-day ($154.94). The long trend is up; the last two weeks are down. Price is 11.6% under the Oct 30 record of $188.50.</li><li><strong>Momentum:</strong> RSI(14) 41.9. Weak, not washed out.</li><li><strong>Ceiling:</strong> Your 2.0 ext $166.89. The Nov 6 bounce failed at $166.79 and the Nov 11 high was $166.75, so it has capped price twice. Above it, the 50-day at $169.10, then your 2.382 at $174.69.</li><li><strong>Floor:</strong> The Nov 10 low of $160.11 held a dollar above your 1.618 at $159.09 (not broken; no daily close under it). Below that, your 1.382 at $154.27 sits with the 200-day.</li><li><strong>Your tested edge:</strong> Not yet. Price and the 50-day are above the 200-day, so it counts as an uptrend, but RSI is 41.9, not under 40.</li><li><strong>Plays:</strong> No open or watching play on XOM in the scorecard.</li><li><strong>My own line, for comparison:</strong> half of the June low ($134.08) to October high ($188.50) run is $161.29. Every close since the drop has held above it.</li><li><strong>Verdict:</strong> Neither side yet. A daily close above $166.89 supports the upside (next $169.10, then $174.69). A daily close below $159.09 supports the downside (next $154.27). The chart agrees with management on the long view (record high on report day, price above a rising 200-day) and disagrees on the short view: the stock gave back 15% from high to low in seven sessions while management was describing margins above the 10-year range.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"what-would-change-this-read\">What would change this read</h3>\n<ul><li>The 2027 plan press release, due this quarter. A cut to the $20B buyback or a capex change would matter more than the Q3 numbers.</li><li>A dated reopening of the Strait of Hormuz, or a clear escalation. Either one moves both sides of the big worry.</li><li>The next report: date not found; management pointed to late January.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"confidence-and-sources\">Confidence and sources</h3>\n<p>Medium-high. Release figures and the quote were read twice in the source research. The normalisation timeline and the capex range each rest on one read. Governance facts come from Exxon's own vote summary, CFO Dive, MarketScreener and Manifest; the lead director and any succession plan were not found. The CEO start date is from MarketScreener only. Bars from Webull are adjusted for dividends.</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://investor.exxonmobil.com/company-information/press-releases/deta